     "search_docs"
    ],
    "approvals": [],
    "answer": "The calibration of the potentiometers of a PSM on your system is described in the documentation passage with the id [doc:calibration/Classic/potentiometers#introduction]. According to this passage, for the calibration process, you need to hold the arm in the zero position. This can be done with the arm powered or not. When powered, you can use the GUI arm widget to control the joints' position and get the arm closed to the zero position. The passage also mentions a simple solution to calibrate the potentiometer offsets for the PSM's last 4 actuators and provides a method to calibrate the PSM's 3rd potentiometer.",
